16	@i_backgrounds:I{ky=~18:target_backgrounds;pr=@project;so=[@s_continuation];st=unresolved;vl=?;wh=@user;wy=~372:The predominant level backgrounds of the side-view game are not stated. The retained comparison sheet showed the navy outline separates the figure on busy mid-value backgrounds but nearly disappears on dark ones, so the outline decision depends on this. The light, dark and busy bands used in the readability criterion are the agent's test set, not the game's backgrounds.}
17	@i_canvas:I{ky=~2:px;pr=@project;so=[@s_brief,@s_refobs];st=unresolved;vl=?;wh=@user;wy=~233:The user has explicitly not chosen the final canvas size. Both references are 32x32 carrying an 18x25 figure, which is an observation about the source art and not an adopted project value. This choice blocks every raster output plan.}
18	@i_design_language:I{ky=~15:design_language;pr=@project;so=[@s_brief,@s_refobs];st=proposed;vl=~257:Carry the flat colour, absent anti-aliasing, binary alpha and blocky low-detail construction of the references into a genuinely side-view figure; treat the front-facing symmetric shape of the references as a style swatch rather than as the character design.;wh=@user;wy=~295:Proposal needing the agreement of the owner. Both references are front-facing and bilaterally symmetric while the stated destination is a side-view game, so the reference pose cannot be reproduced literally. This proposal states which parts of the references are being matched and which are not.}
19	@i_display_scale:I{ky=~13:display_scale;pr=@project;so=[@s_methods];st=unresolved;vl=?;wh=@user;wy=~224:The target on-screen integer zoom is not stated. The bundled integer-presentation method requires a target viewport as an input, and the scale bounds how much interior detail survives, so it interacts with the canvas choice.}
20	@i_engine:I{ky=~6:engine;pr=@project;so=[@s_brief];st=unresolved;vl=?;wh=@user;wy=~112:No destination engine or importer is named, so no engine import acceptance can be performed in this project yet.}
21	@i_outline:I{ky=~14:edge_treatment;pr=@project;so=[@s_brief,@s_refobs,@s_ref_a,@s_ref_b];st=conflict;vl=[~132:reference.png: flat 2px dark outline #25354A fully enclosing the body, also carrying the shoulder bar, base bar and solid top stalks,~70:reference-b.png: no outline, flat teal silhouette with cream eyes only];wh=@user;wy=~409:The user states the references disagree here. Measured: the two files differ in exactly 180 pixels and every difference is #25354A becoming #56B5BC. The outline is load-bearing rather than trim, because removing it also removes the shoulder bar, base bar and stalk interiors. Retained as a conflict; the bundled edge-rhythm method states contour style is authored intent and must not be resolved mechanically.}
22	@i_palette:I{ky=~2:pl;pr=@project;so=[@s_refobs,@s_ref_a,@s_ref_b];st=observed;vl=[~7:#56B5BC,~7:#F4DDA2,~7:#25354A];wh=@user;wy=~248:Measured from the references: teal body, cream eyes, and navy present only in reference.png. Observed, not agreed. Whether #25354A belongs to the output palette depends entirely on the unresolved outline decision, so this cannot be confirmed first.}
23	@i_role_diff:I{ky=~20:role_differentiation;pr=@project;so=[@s_brief,@s_refobs];st=unresolved;vl=?;wh=@user;wy=~271:How a scout reads as a scout and a medic as a medic is not stated, and neither reference carries role-identifying equipment or accent colour. At the detail density of the references this needs a deliberate device, such as a reserved accent hue or a silhouette attachment.}
